# rgb-led-smoke

A portable application whose output is light. It shows red, green, blue, and
white on every LED of the chain, holding each long enough to be named, then
turns a colour wheel through the chain for a few seconds and goes dark.

It names mm.led for the LEDs and mm.mcu for the delay, and no board, SDK, or
vendor: whichever provider the selected board binds is the one it drives. On
the Zero boards that is one WS2812B.

The four solid colours are the check worth making by eye. A controller that
sends the bytes in the wrong order shows green where red belongs and red where
green does, while blue and white stay right. Colours are a quarter of full
scale, which is plainly visible and not uncomfortable at a desk.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Every step passed, and the chain is dark. |
| 1 | initialize failed. |
| 2 | The chain reports no LEDs. |
| 3 | A solid colour could not be written or refreshed. |
| 4 | The colour wheel could not be written or refreshed. |
| 5 | A delay failed. |
| 6 | sleep failed. |
